# s3-07 core wire (CORE-WIRE-G2)

No new module, workspace member, dependency or registration: the task edits computer_user_control.rs only; g25-fu-cu-a also edits computer_backend.rs and computer_lane.rs (parking outside the lane, saved-login steps in the foreground lane).

## The section's idleResumeSeconds (after s3-02's rows are applied)

The field is s3-02's: `ComputerSection.idle_resume_seconds: u32` (mixdog-protocol/src/section.rs, s3-02.rows [type_edits] 5); no
second field is added to `ComputerUserControlSection`. In `mixdog-core/src/run_host/native_tools.rs`, the `ComputerSection { .. }`
literal that publishes the section (the one that sets `user_control: self.control.section()`) takes

    idle_resume_seconds: self.control.idle_resume_seconds(),

in place of the literal `5` s3-02's rows give every literal; the test helper `section` there keeps `5`. `set_idle_resume` already
calls the section listener, so a change is published at once.

## s3-19 (daemon ComputerUserControlService) consumes

- `UserControlState::pause(&self) -> bool` (already existed; its hold now parks requests up to 15 s, then they answer `paused`)
- `UserControlState::take_over_environment(&self, reason: &str) -> bool` (`desktop_unavailable` | `display_changed`)
- `UserControlState::set_idle_resume(&self, seconds: u32)` (the caller rejects values outside 0..60 with
  `computer_idle_seconds_invalid: use 0 or 1..60`; the core holds anything above 60 at 60) and `idle_resume_seconds(&self) -> u32`
- Persistence of the interval (`computer-idle-resume.json`) is the daemon's, not the state's.

## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

Nothing to remove for this task.
